## Why This Is Asked
Assess hands-on orchestration across Azure components during incidents, focusing on tenant isolation, automated rollback safety, and auditable controls.

## Key Concepts
- UEBA-driven automation (Defender for Cloud/Sentinel)
- Per-tenant network isolation (NSG, Private Endpoint)
- Key Vault key rotation and re-encryption
- Token revocation and Conditional Access control
- Canary-based rollback mechanisms
- Centralized auditing and alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator snippet
async function quarantineTenant(tenantId){
  await applyPerTenantNSG(tenantId);
  await rotateKeyVaultKeys(tenantId);
  await revokeTokensAndDisableCA(tenantId);
  await rollbackToLastGoodRelease(tenantId);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical guardrails for multi-tenant data platforms, focusing on secure upgrades and leakage controls in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Lighthouse, per-tenant managed identities, least privilege
- Synapse RLS, Data Lake ACLs, per-tenant isolation
- Key Vault rotation, policy gates for secrets in config
- Canary deployments, feature flags, automated rollback
- UEBA monitoring, incident response, runbooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example guardrail check: ensure secrets aren't in config
function validateConfig(config) {
  const forbidden = ['AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY','AZURE_SQL_PASSWORD','SECRET'];
  for (const k of Object.keys(config)) {
    if (forbidden.includes(k.toUpperCase()) || /password|secret|token/i.test(String(config[k]))) {
      throw new Error('Secrets must be stored in Key Vault and not in config');
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

